WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.560
- From the moment I heard
my next guest's music,

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.770
I was a fan, my mom actually
showed me her record

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.400
and I love her.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.130
I even performed her song, "You Say"

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:10.170
for our first show in quarantine.

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:13.610
Her music is very necessary
for these times, any time,

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:15.380
but it's especially important right now.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:16.860
So let's bring her in here.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:17.760
Hi, Lauren!

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.680
- Hey, Kelly, hey!

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:22.190
- I know the last time
we ran into each other,

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:23.023
we were at dinner.

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:25.080
- You were.
- But I'm such a fan of yours

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.800
and I hope the shows at
the Greek went really well,

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.240
but you had to postpone your tour, right?

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.530
So when do you plan on
kicking that back off, 2021?

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:36.180
- Yes we start back again in 2021

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:41.000
and I am so ready, I'm
telling you, I miss,

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.980
it's like everybody on the
road becomes your family,

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.720
you know, they're like your people

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.440
and so just being apart and being away,

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.270
I'm like, "How much longer?"

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:52.760
I feel like every day feels like

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:55.830
it's 30 hours, not 24 hours, you know,

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:58.400
it's like every day that goes by, gosh,

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.790
I miss the people, I miss the environment,

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:03.630
I miss the energy of
being able to just sing

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:07.510
and have people experience
something collectively together.

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:10.830
I miss the environment and
I miss my friends, you know.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:12.470
- I get it, so tell me about

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:14.667
the song you're gonna
perform, it's called "Rescue".

00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:17.120
- "Rescue" is probably one

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.963
of the most personal songs on the record.

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:25.310
I remember writing it
in mind of a loved one.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:27.760
And the thing about it is,

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.300
I don't know if this has
ever happened to you,

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.630
where you write a song
but it's almost like

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:34.760
the song writes you before you write it,

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.870
I don't know if that makes
sense, but it's like,

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:39.490
especially for times right now,

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:40.990
like especially with what's going on,

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:44.250
it's like that song
couldn't have been more real

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:47.253
and more potent for such a time as this.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.570
But it's like you're experiencing it

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:54.060
with every other person who's listening.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:55.960
But, yeah, I don't know
if that makes sense,

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:58.380
where it's like, you write the song

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:00.290
but the song really writes
you before you write it,

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:03.780
like it's an experience
that is yet to be had,

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:05.150
like you're about to have that experience

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:06.140
but you don't even realize it

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:07.860
and you're just writing and you're writing

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:08.820
and you're enjoying it

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:10.407
and then all of a sudden, it's like,

00:02:10.407 --> 00:02:12.350
"Whoa, this became real." you know?

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:13.653
- I agree, I agree.

